{"k":"bin","t":"Binomial Theorem","cls":"11","u":"Algebra","s":[["Expansion",[{"q":"Binomial theorem","f":"(x+a)^n=\\sum_{r=0}^{n}{}^nC_r\\,x^{n-r}a^r","n":"$n+1$ terms, $n\\in\\mathbb N$.","d":"Induction: assume for $n$, multiply by $(x+a)$, and use ${}^nC_r+{}^nC_{r-1}={}^{n+1}C_r$."},{"q":"General term","f":"T_{r+1}={}^nC_r\\,x^{n-r}a^r"},{"q":"Middle term(s)","f":"n\\ \\text{even}:\\ T_{\\frac n2+1};\\qquad n\\ \\text{odd}:\\ T_{\\frac{n+1}2},\\ T_{\\frac{n+3}2}"},{"q":"Term independent of $x$ in $\\left(x^\\alpha+\\frac1{x^\\beta}\\right)^n$","f":"\\alpha(n-r)-\\beta r=0\\ \\Rightarrow\\ r=\\frac{\\alpha n}{\\alpha+\\beta}"},{"q":"Numerically greatest term in $(1+x)^n$","f":"\\frac{T_{r+1}}{T_r}=\\frac{n-r+1}{r}|x|\\ge1\\iff r\\le\\frac{(n+1)|x|}{1+|x|}","n":"If $m=\\frac{(n+1)|x|}{1+|x|}$ is an integer, $T_m$ and $T_{m+1}$ are equal and greatest; else $T_{[m]+1}$."},{"q":"Number of terms in a multinomial expansion","f":"(x_1+\\cdots+x_r)^n:\\ {}^{n+r-1}C_{r-1}\\ \\text{terms}"},{"q":"Multinomial coefficient","f":"(x_1+\\cdots+x_k)^n=\\sum\\frac{n!}{n_1!\\cdots n_k!}x_1^{n_1}\\cdots x_k^{n_k},\\quad\\sum n_i=n"}]],["Sums of coefficients",[{"q":"Sum of all binomial coefficients","f":"C_0+C_1+\\cdots+C_n=2^n","d":"Put $x=1$ in $(1+x)^n=\\sum C_rx^r$."},{"q":"Alternate sums","f":"C_0+C_2+C_4+\\cdots=C_1+C_3+\\cdots=2^{n-1}","d":"Put $x=-1$: $\\sum(-1)^rC_r=0$; combine with the total $2^n$."},{"q":"Weighted sum $\\sum rC_r$","f":"\\sum_{r=0}^n r\\,C_r=n2^{n-1},\\qquad\\sum r^2C_r=n(n+1)2^{n-2}","d":"Differentiate $(1+x)^n$ and put $x=1$."},{"q":"Sum $\\sum\\frac{C_r}{r+1}$","f":"\\sum_{r=0}^n\\frac{C_r}{r+1}=\\frac{2^{n+1}-1}{n+1}","d":"Integrate $(1+x)^n$ from $0$ to $1$."},{"q":"Alternating version","f":"\\sum_{r=0}^n\\frac{(-1)^rC_r}{r+1}=\\frac1{n+1}"},{"q":"Vandermonde's identity","f":"\\sum_{r}{}^mC_r\\,{}^nC_{k-r}={}^{m+n}C_k","n":"Special: $C_0^2+C_1^2+\\cdots+C_n^2={}^{2n}C_n$.","d":"Compare coefficient of $x^k$ in $(1+x)^m(1+x)^n=(1+x)^{m+n}$."},{"q":"Product sum $\\sum C_rC_{r+k}$","f":"C_0C_k+C_1C_{k+1}+\\cdots+C_{n-k}C_n={}^{2n}C_{n-k}"},{"q":"Alternating squares","f":"C_0^2-C_1^2+C_2^2-\\cdots=\\begin{cases}0,&n\\ \\text{odd}\\\\(-1)^{n/2}\\,{}^nC_{n/2},&n\\ \\text{even}\\end{cases}"},{"q":"Sum of coefficients of a polynomial","f":"f(1);\\qquad\\text{even-power coefficients}=\\frac{f(1)+f(-1)}2"}]],["General index",[{"q":"Binomial theorem for any index","f":"(1+x)^n=1+nx+\\frac{n(n-1)}{2!}x^2+\\cdots,\\quad|x|<1","n":"General term $\\frac{n(n-1)\\cdots(n-r+1)}{r!}x^r$."},{"q":"Standard expansions","f":"(1-x)^{-1}=\\sum x^r,\\quad(1-x)^{-2}=\\sum(r+1)x^r,\\quad(1-x)^{-n}=\\sum{}^{n+r-1}C_r\\,x^r"},{"q":"Approximation for small $x$","f":"(1+x)^n\\approx1+nx"}]],["Common results",[{"q":"Divisibility / remainder trick","f":"(1+a)^n=1+na+\\binom n2a^2+\\cdots\\ \\Rightarrow\\ (1+a)^n\\equiv1+na\\pmod{a^2}","n":"E.g. $7^{2n}=49^n=(1+48)^n$."},{"q":"Integral and fractional part trick","f":"(\\sqrt a+b)^n=I+f,\\ \\ (\\sqrt a-b)^n=f'\\ (0<f'<1):\\ \\ I+f\\pm f'\\ \\text{is an integer}","n":"If $n$ is odd and $\\sqrt a-b>0$, $f=f'$; then $(I+f)f=(a-b^2)^n$."},{"q":"Last digits","f":"\\text{use } (10k\\pm1)^n\\ \\text{expansion modulo } 10, 100"}]]]}